  "id": "Compound::DB00188 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Bortezomib is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected pathways involving metabolic and inflammatory processes. The evidence suggests that Bortezomib exerts a causal effect on Hypermagnesaemia, which in turn is linked to Calcitriol, a hormone that binds to Cyp3a4. Similarly, Bortezomib causes Toxic Skin Eruption, which is associated with Darunavir, another compound that binds to Cyp3a4. These pathways highlight a mechanism by which Bortezomib indirectly influences Cyp3a4 through the activation of downstream metabolites and inflammatory mediators. The shared role of Cyp3a4 in binding to these compounds underscores a potential mechanism of drug-induced metabolic modulation. The integration of these pathways suggests that Bortezomib may modulate Cyp3a4 through a complex interplay of metabolic and inflammatory signals, with Cyp3a4 acting as a central mediator in the drug's effects.",
